Live draw diagnostic: name the caller and the guest state that created each live surface.
Toro's own patch (7xxx), diagnostic only (no behaviour change).
What: the "[surfsz] new live surface" line (first 24 surfaces) now says which path created the surface
(render-target, mrt, blit-dst, display-tile) and the frame, followed by the render-target state (colour format,
antialias mode and sample grid, clip, pitches, offsets, target, zeta) or the blit (source, source surface, pitches,
size). The state is only formatted when a surface is created.
Why: runs tlp-7009b and tlp-7009n-1 (title 3D scene black) both create a second live surface 0:0x1FB0000 at
2560x1440 around frame 770 (116 s), aliasing the 5120x2880 antialiased scene surface at the same address; no run
with a normal title creates it. Which path makes it, and with which state, is not in the log.
Switch: none.
Verify: build; the [surfsz] lines carry "via ..." and an "rt:" or "blit:" line.

